# Runtime / Secrets
dv-control-webapp/config.json
dv-control-webapp/energy_state.json
# A-3 (Go-Live-Review 2026-06-10): the app persists day-energy counters to
# ${DV_DATA_DIR}/energy_state.json, but with no DV_DATA_DIR it falls back to the
# app dir and overwrites the in-repo file — a tracked runtime file makes the tree
# dirty and breaks the `git checkout`-based self-update. Keep it out of git.
dvhub/energy_state.json
# Same DV_DATA_DIR-fallback hazard (A-3): the Pro license state, the not-halt
# (emergency-stop) state and the EOS opt-out marker are written to
# ${DV_DATA_DIR} at runtime (prod: /var/lib/dvhub) but fall back to the app dir
# when DV_DATA_DIR is unset. The operator's license must NEVER be committed and
# must survive a `git checkout`-based self-update — keep all of it out of git.
license_state.json
dvhub/license_state.json
control_state.json
dvhub/control_state.json
.no-eos
eos-provision.log
# Local diagnostic scratch files (background-flow probes, ad-hoc screenshots).
dvhub/diag-*.mjs
dvhub/diag-*.png

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
# Lockfiles are ignored by default, but dvhub's is tracked on purpose: CI runs
# `npm ci` and the actions/setup-node npm cache, both of which require
# dvhub/package-lock.json to exist in the repo (see .github/workflows/ci.yml).
package-lock.json
!dvhub/package-lock.json

